Experiment B — remove only the hash suffix (single-variable control)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Same worktree, one line changed (kernel/limine.conf):

    -    path: boot(1):/NUCLEUS#blake2b:PLACEHOLDER_KERNEL_HASH
    +    path: boot(1):/NUCLEUS

Rebuild + boot:

    rc=124                      # (expected: interactive shell, timeout kill)
    --- serial tail ---
      memmap:    base=0x00000000fd000000 len=0x300000 framebuffer
    NOVA_BOOT_OK
    keyboard:    PS/2 poller ready
    NOVA Nucleus K3 console. Type `help`.
    nova>

Boots to the shell. The `#blake2b:` suffix is the sole cause of the
regular-image regression.

Attribution
-----------
- K3c (this thread) touched neither build-disk.sh, kernel/limine.conf's
  path line, nor any bootchain code; the K3c selftest path still passes
  4/4 on the same HEAD and machine (build/qemu-selftest-serial.log).
- The regression reproduces at C4's HEAD with K3c's kernel absent
  (99,688-byte pre-FAT ELF) and disappears when only the path suffix is
  removed. Therefore C4 introduced it.

Suggested remediation (for the C4 owner — not applied here)
-----------------------------------------------------------
1. Append a real blake2b digest, 128 hex chars, no `blake2b:` prefix:
   `path: boot(1):/NUCLEUS#<digest>` where digest =
   hashlib.blake2b(kernel_elf_bytes, digest_size=64).hexdigest()
   (Python stdlib, no new dependency), or b2sum where available.
2. build-disk.sh must hash the exact file that lands on the ESP, and the
   conf-copy logic must handle the NOVA_TEST=1 / regular switch so the
   substituted config is the one embedded (a stale build/limine.conf from
   a prior selftest build currently leaks into the next regular build).
3. Fix check 5/9 (verify-disk.py / oracle-disk.py fixtures) to expect the
   substituted length, or compare against the substituted file rather
   than the raw kernel/limine.conf — currently "520 == 479" fails even
   when the substitution is correct in shape.
4. decide_policy.md / progress.md say "C4 verified" (284e4d6); that
   verification did not include a boot of the regular image, or the
   panic would have been seen. The regular-image QEMU cases in
   scripts/check.sh stage 8 are the missing check.

