RESOLUTION (appended 2026-09-27, same day — see progress.md top entry)
======================================================================
Repaired the same day by the follow-up C4-fix work order. Item 1 and 2 of
the sketch above are implemented exactly: kernel/limine.conf now carries
#KERNEL_BLAKE2B_512_PLACEHOLDER (no prefix), build-disk.sh substitutes a
real 128-hex blake2b-512 digest (hashlib, digest_size=64) of the exact ELF
that lands on the ESP into a per-image sidecar build/limine.conf.<image>
(stale-shared-build/limine.conf leak eliminated; substitution failure is
fatal). Item 3: verify-disk.py / fuzz-disk.py / oracle-disk.py take the
embedded-config expectation from the sidecar (missing or stale sidecar
exits 1 loudly), plus a new verifier section 7 re-derives the digest from
the build-input kernel. All 4 QEMU boot cases PASS — Limine's own hash
verification accepts the real digest; stage 5 is 52 checks; stage 6 fuzz
PASS. Evidence: docs/logs/c4fix-check-full.log and
docs/logs/c4fix-mutation-and-negative-tests.log. Item 4 (the 2026-09-26
"verified" claim) stands as written: regular-image boots were not part of
that verification.
